{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Strengthen the Serious Violence Duty to Help Keep Young People Safe",
        "additional_details": "The Government must strengthen the Serious Violence Duty by ensuring:\r\n \r\n\u2022 Safe youth spaces in every community.\r\n\u2022 Early intervention for young people at risk.\r\n\u2022 Long-term funding for prevention.\r\n\u2022 Transparency on local prevention efforts and outcomes.\r\n\u2022 A meaningful voice for affected young people and families.\r\n \r\nWe cannot wait until a child is injured, exploited or killed before acting.  Prevention must come before tragedy. We've had enough children dying. Enough families bereaved. Enough funerals. This should be done in memory of Jamal.",
        "background": "We call on the UK Government to strengthen the statutory Serious Violence Duty by introducing minimum national standards for youth violence prevention, including access to safe youth spaces, early intervention, mentoring and community-based prevention programmes.",
